Z||000004||Eric_PA||05-05-2001||10:16 AM||||I am having my flywheel modified and ballanced by Chris West. It's for a 3800, but if he can get that done, I'm sure it wouldn't be a problem to moddify a flywheel to work with the caddy engine. I sent him the flex plate to the 3800 and supplied a new 85 to 87 fiero flywheel. here's the web site. <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Engine_hardware/Engine_hardware.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Engine_hardware/Engine_hardware.html</A> <P>Eric<p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 05-05-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||Howard_Sacks||05-05-2001||11:55 AM||||I'm also having Chris West do my flywheel.  Once I get out of school and back into South Jersey I'm pulling the flywheel off of my 2.8 and having him modify it for the caddy V8.||||reg||1
Z||000006||bubbajoexx||05-06-2001||06:50 PM||||for those of you modifing flywheels for the caddy swap the fiero flywheel is no good you must use the Z24 or any front drive 2.8 or 3.1 they are nuetral balance and will work on the caddy engine the fiero is external balanced and there for no good to you<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000007||PBJ||05-06-2001||07:37 PM||||If you need to use the above specified flywheels, what clutch and pressure disc do you use? Does the clutch for 86 4sp bolt onto the neutral balance z24 type flywheel and work ok with 4spd?||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||05-07-2001||07:32 AM||||Just out of curiosity, can't you just re-balance the 84-87 flywheels and make them neutral? After you plug and re-drill, wouldn't you have to re-balance anyway? I've heard (can't confirm) that the Z24 flywheel is several pounds heaver than the Fiero and I would hate to add more rotating mass.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000009||Will||05-07-2001||10:23 AM||||The balancing weight is cast onto the back of the flywheel. It's easy to see and almost as easy to grind off.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BigTurbo87GT||05-07-2001||11:13 AM||||The Fiero Shop can make a flywheel anyway you like. They are willing to fab an aluminum flywheel for me (Northstar 4.6 to Getrag). And can most likely do it by speck, i.e. you don't have to send them old pieces.<BR>Of course this ain't cheap ;-)||||reg||1
Z||000011||northstar87||05-07-2001||12:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bubbajoexx:<BR><B>for those of you modifing flywheels for the caddy swap the fiero flywheel is no good you must use the Z24 or any front drive 2.8 or 3.1 they are nuetral balance and will work on the caddy engine the fiero is external balanced and there for no good to you</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 1988 Fiero V-6 5 speed flywheel is nuetral balanced.  You can modify that one.<P>Chris Moore<BR>ASE Master Auto Tech and Auto Instructor<BR>1986 GT Convertible Northstar<BR>1987 GT Northstar<BR>1988 T-TOP 3.4 5 speed<BR>1988 T-TOP Stock||||reg||1
Z||000012||NPlack||05-07-2001||01:40 PM||||What cad motor are you swapping in?  A 425/472/500?  I am very interested in this, as the thought has crossed my mind.  I currently have a 1970 Cadillac Deville with the 472 Cadillac motor.  Due to the bad gas mileage, and prices, (12MPG on 91 Octane Premium), I have begun to look for a good fiero.  I always like cars that are out of the ordianry.  Both my cad and a Fiero fit this description.<P>Okay i am rambling, sorry.  What kind of drivetrain will be behind this motor?  Manual or automatic?  I have limited knowledge of the fiero drivetrain, so how is the tranny attached to the gearbox/rearend/whatever?  Can a 700-R4 or equivalent be swapped in?  OD would be nice.  Any insight to this would be appriciated.  Also what kind of gears are used in the fiero rear?  Can they be pruchased somehwere to swap ratios?<P>If you have any questions on the cad motor, feel free to ask me.  Also two great sites for teh Big Cad motors is <A HREF="http://www.500cid.com" TARGET=_blank>www.500cid.com</A>  and a GREAT messageboard is members.boardhost.com/BadCad/ (Caps ARE important!!!).<P>-Plack||||reg||1
Z||000013||NPlack||05-07-2001||01:44 PM||||My bad!  Just looked at the Reply's in more detail!  Northstar not the Big Cad.  Anyways, i would still like to know about the fiero tranny's and rears.  I know that the auto is the TH-125, and there were munsie/getrag 4's and 5's, and the crappy Isusu tranny.  Can any other tranny's be used, or are they a special unit for the fiero?<P>-Plack||||reg||1
Z||000014||94ZonCrack||05-07-2001||01:48 PM||||I'm swapping in the 4.1L v8 from an 87 Eldorado. Yeah I know it's way low on hp. I plan on giving it a 100hp shot of nitrous.<P>Got all then info from <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000015||NPlack||05-07-2001||04:01 PM||||OK!!!  IT ALL MAKES SENSE NOW!!!  Thanks for that link!  I helped a bunch.  So the Fiero is basically like a VW Bug (ouch, hate to lower it to that for the comparison) in the way the drivetrain is.  Basically a FWD motor in the rear rather than the front.<P>Okay, so in the swap, can the Motor *AND* transmission be used from the cadillac?  I would like to get O/D automatic.  (fuel economy is the reason for this project).  Are all of the axles and CV joints the same?<P>-Plack||||reg||1
