Z||000017||bubbajoexx||05-07-2001||08:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B>Just out of curiosity, can't you just re-balance the 84-87 flywheels and make them neutral? After you plug and re-drill, wouldn't you have to re-balance anyway? I've heard (can't confirm) that the Z24 flywheel is several pounds heaver than the Fiero and I would hate to add more rotating mass.<P>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>no rebalancing needed the plugs are all of equal size and weight ||||reg||1
